course: dictionary
lesson: 8456
title: Sailor: a person who works on a boat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sailor is a person who works on a ship or boat, especially as part of its crew. A sailor can also be a member of a navy, or a person who sails boats for fun or sport. Read the words around the word to find which meaning fits.
explain: «Real sailors did bring parrots home from tropical voyages.» A voyage is a long trip by sea, so sailors here are people who work on a ship. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A person who works on a ship fits. A person who bakes bread does not.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «A good sailor» means a person who does not feel seasick on a boat, which is a different sense again. Put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A sailor is a person who works on a ship or boat, especially as part of its crew.
fact: A sailor can be a member of a navy.
fact: A sailor can also be a person who sails boats for fun or sport.
fact: «A magnetised needle on a leaf floating in water turns to point north; sailors used compasses like this nearly a thousand years ago.»
fact: Water safety means wearing a life jacket when you sail.
exercise: «A magnetised needle on a leaf floating in water turns to point north.» Sailors used this to find north. What was it? | A life jacket | *A compass | A telescope | A sailor's knot
exercise: Sam sails his small boat on the lake for fun. What is Sam? | A baker | A parrot | A carpenter | *A sailor
exercise: «John Harrison, a carpenter born in Yorkshire, built sea clocks that kept good time on rolling ships.» What was John Harrison's job? | A dentist | A cook | *A carpenter | A sailor
test: A sailor who is a member of a navy serves in which kind of group? | A choir | *A navy | A bakery | A library
test: «Mia was a good sailor and never felt sick on the boat.» What does good sailor mean here? | A person who makes boats | A person who runs very fast | A person who loves cake | *A person who does not get seasick
exam: «The clever sailor cut his raft into a grating and jammed it in the Whale's throat.» What does sailor mean in this sentence? | A kind of whale | A hat worn in the sun | *A person who works on a ship or boat | A sort of bird
